
<p>Emine Yücel, reporting for TPM:</p>

<blockquote>
  <p>Mississippi prosecutor Scott Colom officially defeated incumbent
Sen. Cindy Hyde-Smith (R-MS) Wednesday night. Colom will be the
first Democrat to represent Mississippi in the Senate since 1982
and he will also become the state’s first Black senator in nearly
150 years.</p>
</blockquote>

<p>150 years is, needless to say, a long time. The crazy part about that is that <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/African_Americans_in_Mississippi">Mississippi has the highest proportion of black citizens</a> in the entire country (38 percent).</p>

<p>Colom, by all accounts, ran a fantastic campaign, with little to no support from the national Democratic Party because almost no one imagined Mississippi — the deepest of the deep South — might turn blue. <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Nga2Q207-58">This commercial Colom ran</a> is one of the best I’ve ever seen. Not just best <em>political</em> commercials. I mean it’s one of the best 30-second spots ever made. It’s perfect. I just keep watching it over and over.</p>

<p><strong>Update:</strong> I stand corrected on the national support. <a href="https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/mississippi-election-democrats-fundraising-ec77cb8a?st=KixCU4">The WSJ ran a story back in September</a> — six weeks before the election — on Senate Minority Leader Chuck Schumer raising funds for Colom amongst big Democratic donors. Schumer smelled a winner.</p>

